Most people will hear that the BoC held at 2.25% and move on. What will actually matter is the language in the statement about whether a rate hike is still on the table, what the Bank says about the ceasefire''s impact on the inflation outlook, and how it characterizes a labour market where private sector hiring has been contracting all year.<br><br>
If you have any decisions pending that depend on rate direction, whether a mortgage renewal, a bond portfolio rebalance, or a business borrowing decision, the next five days are worth paying attention to carefully.<br><br>
I would be glad to walk through what the data means for your situation specifically.<br><br>
